    "algorithm": "1. Read DiversitySet and its source-bound shared raw-input/owner constraints. Verify each member own authorized program/profile; evaluate each candidate required intrinsic geometry/use against that program. Any proved member violation remains a member failure; missing authorization/evidence yields UNKNOWN.\n2. Enumerate exactly k*(k-1)/2 unordered whole-plan pairs. Do not discard a pair because authorized bedroom programs differ.\n3. Build role graphs for each member with core/unit partition, actual room/portal/access graph, source-bound bedroom/occupancy program and frontage allocation. Apply TOPOLOGY_CANONICAL D4 and role-preserving ID permutations; programme attributes cannot be erased to manufacture equivalence.\n4. If programs differ under source-authorized bedroom/program relation and both candidates are valid under their own program plus shared constraints, record the exact differing program attributes as a permitted semantic diversity witness. This is a diversity claim only, not superiority or same-program capacity comparison.\n5. For equal programs, or additional organizational differences, compare canonical topology/function schemas; colors/IDs/seed/mirror-only or numerical jitter without changed relations never count. Unsupported cross-program graph/functional relation yields UNKNOWN for that pair, not INVALID_BRIEF/invalid candidate.\n6. Count only options whose applicable member checks and all required distinctness pairs have complete witnesses. Up to six is not a guarantee. Unknown pair coverage cannot be filled with a fake option. No program reduction is authorized as repair merely to obtain difference."
